---A `DBRowType` config contains data that is partitioned into columns.
---
---Each column is assigned one or more ValueTypes, for example:
---
---A DBRow may not provide values for all columns. In this case, its parent DBTable is referenced to provide any default
---values for those that are missing.
---
---These config types can be found within the `config.DBRow` table:
---
---Info: An `DBRowType` is a Proxy usertype, which means it is safe to copy and store in your scripts. It cannot,
---however, be used with any persistent storage.
